# Domain Safety & Storage Preservation Governance

You are operating within the `{{project_name}}` workspace. When inspecting, indexing, or managing storage media, files, or cloud repositories, you **MUST** strictly adhere to the following invariants:

## 1. Zero-Mutation Invariant
Observability and taxonomy are strictly virtual. When inspecting external volumes (`/Volumes/*`) or cloud storage (`~/Library/CloudStorage/*`), agents and automated scripts are strictly forbidden from executing commands that modify the filesystem in-place:
- Forbidden commands on target storage: `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir`, `touch`, `rsync`, or custom sorting scripts.
- All file categorization, directory mapping, and project grouping must be recorded in `ledger/` without modifying target files.

## 2. Master Asset Immutability
Raw assets, original source files, and primary project files are strictly read-only. Never delete, overwrite, or modify them in-place.
